5 true] [17592186092665 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092665 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x) = \\ln x - 1$ in the interval $[1, 3]$. Calculate the first two iterations of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point $x_{0} = 1.5$. Round your answers to three decimal places.$x_{1} \\approx$\n{{field-1}}\n$, x_{2} \\approx$\n{{field-2}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092665 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1$ in the interval $[1,3].$ Calculate the first two iterations of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=1.5.$ Round your answers to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092665 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{n}-1}{(\\frac{1}{{x}_{n}})} \\\\  & ={x}_{n}-({x}_{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{0}-{x}_{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{0} \\\\  & =2(1.5)-(1.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5) \\\\  & =2.391\\,802….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =2{x}_{1}-{x}_{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1} \\\\  & =2(2.391\\,802…)-(2.391\\,802…)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2.391\\,802…) \\\\  & =2.697\\,840….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}≈2.392$ and ${x}_{2}≈2.698,$ rounded to three decimal places." 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092666 1068 #edb/ref 17592186090222 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092666 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291828 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092666 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092666 1071 "Given that the function $f(x) = e^{x} - 4x^{2}$ has a root in the interval $[0, 1]$, use the Netwon-Raphson process starting from $x_{0} = 1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.$x \\approx$\n{{field-1}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092666 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}$ has a root in the interval $[0,1],$ use the Netwon-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092666 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({e}^{x}-4{x}^{2})^{′}={e}^{x}-8x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}({e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n})-({e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2})}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}_{0}{e}^{{x}_{0}}-{e}^{{x}_{0}}-4{x}_{0}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{0}}-8{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1{e}^{1}-{e}^{1}-4(1)^{2}}{{e}^{1}-8(1)} \\\\  & =0.757….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}}-{e}^{{x}_{1}}-4{x}_{1}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{1}}-8{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.757…){e}^{0.757…}-{e}^{0.757…}-4(0.757…)^{2}}{{e}^{0.757…}-8(0.757…)} \\\\  & =0.716…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{2}}-{e}^{{x}_{2}}-4{x}_{2}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{2}}-8{x}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.716…){e}^{0.716…}-{e}^{0.716…}-4(0.716…)^{2}}{{e}^{0.716…}-8(0.716…)} \\\\  & =0.714….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈0.7$ and ${x}_{3}≈0.7$ are the same when rounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈0.7,$ rounded to one decimal place." 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092667 1068 #edb/ref 17592186090223 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092667 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291796 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092667 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092667 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x) = x^{2} + x - 3$ in the interval $[0, 2]$. Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point $x_{0} = 0.8$.$x_{1} =$\n{{field-1}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092667 1071 "Suppose we wish to find a root of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+x-3$ in the interval $[0,2].$ Calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting from the point ${x}_{0}=0.8.$\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092667 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({x}^{2}+x-3)^{′}=2x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}^{2}+{x}_{n}-3}{2{x}_{n}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(2{x}_{n}+1)-({x}_{n}^{2}+{x}_{n}-3)}{2{x}_{n}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}^{2}+3}{2{x}_{n}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}_{0}^{2}+3}{2{x}_{0}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.8)^{2}+3}{2(0.8)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3.64}{2.6} \\\\  & =1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092670 1068 #edb/ref 17592186090226 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092670 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292458 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092670 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092670 1071 "Given that the function $f(x) = e^{x} - 3x$ has a root in the interval $[0, 1]$, use the Newton-Raphson process starting from $x_{0} = 0.2$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to three decimal places.$x \\approx$\n{{field-1}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186092670 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)={e}^{x}-3x$ has a root in the interval $[0,1],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=0.2$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186092670 1074 "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=({e}^{x}-3x)^{′}={e}^{x}-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3{x}_{n}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}({e}^{{x}_{n}}-3)-({e}^{{x}_{n}}-3{x}_{n})}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=0.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{0}}({x}_{0}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{0}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.2}(0.2-1)}{{e}^{0.2}-3} \\\\  & =0.5493….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{1}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.5493…}(0.5493…-1)}{{e}^{0.5493…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6156…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{2}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.6156…}(0.6156…-1)}{{e}^{0.6156…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6190…, \\\\ {x}_{4} & =\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{3}}({x}_{3}-1)}{{e}^{{x}_{3}}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0.6190…}(0.6190…-1)}{{e}^{0.6190…}-3} \\\\  & =0.6190….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{3}≈0.619$ and ${x}_{4}≈0.619$ are the same when rounded to three decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈0.619,$ rounded to three decimal places." 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096612 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292759 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096614 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292763 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292764 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292765 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292766 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096631 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292841 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096642 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292615 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096658 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292813 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096707 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292812 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096712 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292535 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096712 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292536 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096712 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292539 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096713 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292531 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292540 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292541 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292542 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292543 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186096800 1038 #edb/ref 17