e relations are first-order?\n\n1. $a_{n} = 2a_{n - 2}$\n2. $b_{n} = b_{n - 1}^{2} + 2b_{n - 2}$\n3. $c_{n} = 2c_{n - 1} + n$" 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186129573 1074 "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186129574 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126891 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186129574 1068 #edb/ref 17592186291918 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186129574 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186129574 1071 "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3{a}_{n-1}+2{a}_{n-2},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,{a}_{2}=4,\\,n\\ge 3.\n$$" 13194139533409 17592186045585 true] [17592186129574 1071 "Find the fourth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n$a_{n} = 3a_{n - 1} + 2a_{n - 2}, a_{1} = 2, a_{2} = 4, n \\ge 3$." 13194139533409 17592186045585 false] [17592186129574 1074 "Starting with the initial terms ${a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{2}=4,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =4 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3{a}_{2}+2{a}_{1}=3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2=12+4=16 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3{a}_{3}+2{a}_{2}=3\\cdot 16+2\\cdot 4=48+8=56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=56.$" 131